__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.env

# A repair tick's HEAD snapshot, written INTO this tree as scratch.
#
# bin/auto-round stops a submit run outright when `git status --porcelain` is
# non-empty, and --porcelain lists untracked files. So one stray scratch file
# is not a warning: with the repair lock free it reads as "dirty tree with NO
# repair running" and every poll from then on holds. The tree is otherwise
# clean and shippable, HEAD is fresh, the window opens and closes un-entered,
# and nothing in the feed says why beyond "dirty".
#
# Found 2026-08-21T20:41Z: GIT_HEAD.txt had been sitting untracked since at
# least 20:09 holding a stale `ce337ad` and nothing in the pipeline reads it.
# The file is deleted; this entry stops the same shape recurring, because a
# tick that drops one again would re-wedge the gate silently.
#
# This does NOT weaken the gate. What the gate protects is "the working tree
# differs from the branch head that would be submitted" -- an ignored scratch
# file was never part of what ships, so it cannot be that difference. Kept to
# this exact name rather than a wildcard: a broad rule would hide real
# uncommitted work, which is the thing the gate is actually for.
/GIT_HEAD.txt
